WEBVTT

00:00:00.314 --> 00:00:02.745
The copilot is a LangGraph state machine.

00:00:02.785 --> 00:00:04.909
This diagram isn't drawn by hand.

00:00:04.949 --> 00:00:07.883
It's generated from the compiled
graph's own edge list,

00:00:07.923 --> 00:00:10.986
the same list the app
serves, and the tests read.

00:00:14.591 --> 00:00:16.282
Here's the whole safety argument.

00:00:16.322 --> 00:00:19.215
Apply, the only node
that touches equipment,

00:00:19.255 --> 00:00:21.990
has exactly one way in, from confirm.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.602
And confirm is an interrupt:

00:00:23.642 --> 00:00:26.580
the run stops there,
and waits for a person.

00:00:27.251 --> 00:00:29.200
A test walks the graph from the start,

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.267
refuses to pass through confirm,

00:00:31.307 --> 00:00:33.414
and proves that apply is unreachable.

00:00:35.889 --> 00:00:37.420
Then it proposes the plan.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:41.157
The server dry-runs every command
again before the operator sees it,

00:00:41.197 --> 00:00:43.075
and the run suspends at confirm.

00:00:43.115 --> 00:00:46.165
Forty-two seconds in,
the state is checkpointed,

00:00:46.205 --> 00:00:47.958
and nothing has been applied.

00:00:50.973 --> 00:00:52.402
The operator approves.

00:00:52.442 --> 00:00:55.489
That's a new request,
resuming the suspended run.

00:00:55.529 --> 00:00:58.598
Only now does the graph
take the edge into apply.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:05.132
Apply uses the same control
endpoint a human click does,

00:01:05.172 --> 00:01:08.632
as the approving user, marked
as proposed by the copilot.

00:01:08.672 --> 00:01:10.969
The envelope checks each command again,

00:01:11.009 --> 00:01:14.074
and the gateway collected
all four within six seconds.

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.594
And what it isn't.
The checkpointer is in memory,

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:22.064
so a restart forgets a suspended plan.

00:01:22.104 --> 00:01:23.999
The gateway here is a simulator,

00:01:24.039 --> 00:01:26.215
not a real building management system.

00:01:26.255 --> 00:01:28.070
And it proposes setpoints.

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:30.147
It doesn't optimise the building.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:36.562
DTwin. The copilot
proposes. A person approves.

